{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal, due to its inappropriate scale, design, and placement within the dwelling plot, would result in a bulky, cramped, and contrived dwelling. The proposal would harm the character and appearance of the surrounding area, contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture), SC1 (Housing Growth), and SC4 (Scale and Intensity of New Housing Development), and London Plan policies D4 (Delivering Good Design) and D6 (Housing Quality and Standards).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed detached garage, due to its excessive size and scale, as well as its inappropriate location, would create a bulky and incongruous addition to the site. It would fail to appear subordinate to the main dwelling and would harm the character and appearance of the surrounding area, contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 (Context and Character) and CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture).",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development would fail to provide an acceptable internal and external standard of accommodation for the occupiers of the new dwelling due to the inadequate size of one bedroom and insufficient external amenity space, contrary to Local Plan Policy SC5 (Ensuring suitable internal and external space) and the NDSS (Nationally Described Space Standard).",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposal would fail to promote sustainable modes of transport and result in conditions prejudicial to the free flow and safety of pedestrian and vehicular movements due to the excessive car parking provision, the introduction of two crossovers, insufficient pedestrian and vehicular access arrangements and visibility splays. Therefore, the proposal would be contrary to London Plan policy T6.1 and Local Plan policy EC2, as well as the Council's adopted Residential Crossover and Off-Street Parking Policy.",
    "Reason : 5 - The proposal fails to make the fullest contribution to minimising carbon dioxide emissions and fails to demonstrate that the development would maximise energy savings at each step of the energy hierarchy, contrary to Local Plan Policies EQ1 (Energy and Carbon Reduction) and EQ2 (Sustainable design and construction) and London Plan Policies SI2 (Minimising Greenhouse Gas Emissions)."
  ],
